WEBVTT

00:00:07.967 --> 00:00:09.887
And how far back is she now?

00:00:10.007 --> 00:00:12.207
-CREW CHIEF: Look behind you.
-What?

00:00:12.287 --> 00:00:14.127
-Good evening, Storm!
-Wait, how did you--

00:00:14.207 --> 00:00:15.807
Just back here drafting on your butt.

00:00:15.887 --> 00:00:17.127
Nothing to be concerned about.

00:00:17.407 --> 00:00:19.487
Like two June bugs on a summer night.

00:00:19.527 --> 00:00:20.527
(SMOKEY LAUGHS)

00:00:22.967 --> 00:00:25.047
(CHUCKLING) Hey, Hamilton.

00:00:25.087 --> 00:00:27.047
-HAMILTON: Hamilton here.
-Call out our speed.

00:00:27.207 --> 00:00:30.327
208 miles per hour, 207 miles--

00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:32.487
Would you stop that?
You're taking me off my line!

00:00:32.687 --> 00:00:34.647
-Last lap!
-Come on, Cruz!

00:00:35.967 --> 00:00:37.767
CRUZ: Oh-oh!

00:00:37.967 --> 00:00:41.247
My GPS is saying
I have slow traffic in my way.

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:44.247
-No, you are not winning this!
-Ah, you're angry.

00:00:44.487 --> 00:00:46.207
I am not angry!

00:00:46.607 --> 00:00:48.807
You know, you can use that
anger to push through.

00:00:49.087 --> 00:00:50.127
I said I'm not angry!

00:00:51.407 --> 00:00:54.367
Oh, I don't think so! No!

00:00:54.567 --> 00:00:55.887
(CRUZ GRUNTS AND GASPS)

00:00:58.487 --> 00:00:59.607
Cruz, get out of there!

00:00:59.887 --> 00:01:02.447
You don't belong on this track!

00:01:03.807 --> 00:01:06.087
Yes, I do!

00:01:18.407 --> 00:01:21.447
CUTLASS: I don't believe it.
It's Cruz Ramirez for the win!

00:01:21.607 --> 00:01:22.927
DARRELL: I am speechless!

00:01:22.967 --> 00:01:24.367
(ALL CHEERING)

00:01:24.727 --> 00:01:27.407
-(WHOOPING)
-MATER: Nice finish, Cruz! You done it!

00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:29.647
Cruz Ramirez!

00:01:29.887 --> 00:01:31.967
-Yeah, there you go!
-Way to go, Cruz!

00:01:32.287 --> 00:01:33.687
Oh, yes!

00:01:33.967 --> 00:01:35.447
Whoo-hoo!

00:01:40.607 --> 00:01:42.487
Man, heck of a win!

00:01:43.847 --> 00:01:46.807
Yeah. Heck of a win.

00:01:48.087 --> 00:01:49.967
(CROWD CHEERING)

00:01:50.927 --> 00:01:52.647
Hey, Cruz! You were flying!

00:01:52.727 --> 00:01:53.807
Thanks.

00:01:53.887 --> 00:01:54.927
You really had it rolling today.

00:01:54.967 --> 00:01:56.287
-That was cool.
-Thank you!

00:01:56.367 --> 00:01:58.127
Hey, Cruz, your blinker's on.

00:01:58.207 --> 00:02:03.007
It is? Oh! You got me!
Very funny! (LAUGHS)

00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:10.767
CROWD: (CHANTING)
Cruz! Cruz! Cruz!

00:02:10.807 --> 00:02:11.967
MALE FAN 1: Ramirez!

00:02:12.207 --> 00:02:13.287
Whoo!

00:02:13.327 --> 00:02:14.927
MALE FAN 2: Way to go, Cruz!

00:02:16.367 --> 00:02:18.527
Go ahead. Give them some smoke.

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:21.607
(CROWD CONTINUES CHANTING)
Cruz! Cruz! Cruz!

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:23.487
(LAUGHING)

00:02:28.007 --> 00:02:30.527
(LAUGHS AND COUGHS)

00:02:32.887 --> 00:02:34.527
(CHUCKLES) You'll get used to that.

00:02:34.607 --> 00:02:36.807
STERLING: Out of my way!
Come on! Move it! Move!

00:02:37.287 --> 00:02:40.527
Cruz! I knew you had something.

00:02:40.607 --> 00:02:42.887
And now look at you... a winner.

00:02:43.647 --> 00:02:46.687
I could use you as a racer
on our team. We could make--

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:49.807
Sorry, Mr. Sterling.
I would never race for you.

00:02:50.487 --> 00:02:51.527
I quit.

00:02:52.207 --> 00:02:53.687
(HORN HONKING MELODIOUSLY)
Well, then race for me!

00:02:53.847 --> 00:02:54.847
Tex!

00:02:55.287 --> 00:02:57.007
Miss Cruz, I would be tickled pink

00:02:57.047 --> 00:02:59.047
to have you race for team Dinoco.

00:02:59.207 --> 00:03:01.927
As you know, we have a long
history of great racers,

00:03:02.007 --> 00:03:03.367
except for Cal.

00:03:03.527 --> 00:03:05.647
Uh, guys, I'm still right here.

00:03:05.887 --> 00:03:07.647
Team Dinoco, Cruz!

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:09.167
Hire her. I don't care.

00:03:09.327 --> 00:03:11.047
Lightning, now that you're retired...

00:03:11.207 --> 00:03:14.007
I need you first thing Monday
morning for a photo shoot.

00:03:14.567 --> 00:03:16.047
Yeah, all right, Mr. Sterling.

00:03:16.087 --> 00:03:18.047
Whoa! Hang on now.

00:03:19.727 --> 00:03:21.007
(CROWD CHEERING)

00:03:21.047 --> 00:03:23.527
McQUEEN: What?
Why is my name up there?

00:03:23.807 --> 00:03:26.127
You started the race.
That's how it works.

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:27.647
Wait, wait, now-- Wait a minute. No!

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:30.207
Lightning wins, he decides
when he's done racing.

00:03:30.247 --> 00:03:31.607
That was the deal.

00:03:31.687 --> 00:03:33.087
Hi, I'm his lawyer.

00:03:33.167 --> 00:03:34.567
That was the deal.

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:36.367
You are not a nice guy.

00:03:36.407 --> 00:03:37.487
Although, I got to say,

00:03:37.567 --> 00:03:40.407
you do make a quality mudflap
at an affordable price.

00:03:40.487 --> 00:03:42.367
(CLEARS THROAT) Hey, Sterling.

00:03:42.407 --> 00:03:44.767
Why don't you and I
take a drive and talk?

00:03:44.847 --> 00:03:46.607
Billionaire to billionaire.

00:03:46.807 --> 00:03:47.927
-(REPORTERS CLAMORING)
-Cruz, over here.

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:49.487
Just one picture. How does it
feel to beat Jackson Storm?

00:03:49.567 --> 00:03:50.767
-(LAUGHS)
-Take us through it,

00:03:50.847 --> 00:03:52.407
-lap by lap.
-(CAMERAS FLASHING)

00:03:52.447 --> 00:03:55.327
It was great! Uh, didn't expect this.

00:03:55.847 --> 00:03:57.207
(LAUGHS)

00:03:59.407 --> 00:04:02.007
Kid's got a lot of stuff, eh, Doc?

00:04:04.287 --> 00:04:06.407
Well, she had a great teacher.

00:04:07.967 --> 00:04:10.887
And now you get to decide
when you're done racing.

00:04:11.527 --> 00:04:14.167
So what's it gonna be, Stinky?
Uh, Stickers.

00:04:16.447 --> 00:04:18.447
(CHUCKLES)
Oh, I'm gonna keep racing.

00:04:18.527 --> 00:04:21.727
But before that,
I got something I want to do.

00:04:28.967 --> 00:04:31.967
Welcome all to historic Willy's Butte

00:04:32.047 --> 00:04:35.047
for today's great exhibition of speed!

00:04:35.127 --> 00:04:36.287
(ENGINES REVVING)

00:04:36.647 --> 00:04:37.807
(WHOOPS) There she is! Cruz!

00:04:37.847 --> 00:04:39.327
Oh, I love it. I love it. I love it.

00:04:39.487 --> 00:04:40.287
(LAUGHS) Thanks, guys!

00:04:40.527 --> 00:04:42.247
Nice paint, kiddo.

00:04:42.447 --> 00:04:43.927
Pardon me. Big hat, coming through.

00:04:43.967 --> 00:04:46.927
Get 'er done, 51! Whoo-hoo!

00:04:47.087 --> 00:04:49.647
Great number. Was McQueen's idea.

00:04:49.807 --> 00:04:51.727
He felt Hud would've
wanted you to have it.

00:04:52.247 --> 00:04:53.647
I love it.

00:04:53.847 --> 00:04:55.927
Oh, it's perfect. It's very old-school.

00:04:56.127 --> 00:04:58.367
McQUEEN: Did someone
just say old-school?

00:04:59.407 --> 00:05:01.287
NASH: Whoo-hoo! Yeah!

00:05:01.447 --> 00:05:02.807
FAN: Oh, yeah! I like that.
It's bright, but I like it.

00:05:02.847 --> 00:05:04.407
(ALL CHEERING)

00:05:06.367 --> 00:05:09.007
FLO: Looking fabulous.
LUIGI: Favoloso.

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:12.167
-(LAUGHS)
-Trying something new. I like it.

00:05:12.687 --> 00:05:14.607
Wow. Subtle.

00:05:14.807 --> 00:05:18.527
Figured if I'm gonna be your crew chief,
I better do it in style.

00:05:18.687 --> 00:05:20.647
What's Mr. Sterling gonna say?

00:05:20.807 --> 00:05:21.887
I'm actually more worried

00:05:21.967 --> 00:05:24.127
about what Tex is gonna say,
considering he, uh...

00:05:24.287 --> 00:05:27.247
bought Rust-eze. Thanks, Tex!

00:05:27.687 --> 00:05:29.847
(HORN HONKING MELODIOUSLY)
I made that Sterling fella

00:05:29.887 --> 00:05:31.687
a Texas-sized offer!

00:05:32.207 --> 00:05:33.967
So, you ready to start training?

00:05:34.127 --> 00:05:36.047
I don't know. You ready to lose again?

00:05:36.247 --> 00:05:38.567
Oh! Hope you've got your fluffy cloud.

00:05:38.727 --> 00:05:39.967
I hope you got your drip pan.

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:42.727
Got my drip pan and I've taken my nap.

00:05:42.807 --> 00:05:44.167
Bring it on, old man.

00:05:44.207 --> 00:05:45.647
-Luigi.
-Go! Whoo-hoo!

00:05:45.887 --> 00:05:47.087
